From: David Hildenbrand <david@redhat.com>
Subject: mm/ksm: page_remove_rmap() -> folio_remove_rmap_pte()
Date: Wed, 20 Dec 2023 23:44:51 +0100

Let's convert replace_page().

Link: https://lkml.kernel.org/r/20231220224504.646757-28-david@redhat.com
Signed-off-by: David Hildenbrand <david@redhat.com>
Cc: Hugh Dickins <hughd@google.com>
Cc: Matthew Wilcox (Oracle) <willy@infradead.org>
Cc: Muchun Song <muchun.song@linux.dev>
Cc: Muchun Song <songmuchun@bytedance.com>
Cc: Peter Xu <peterx@redhat.com>
Cc: Ryan Roberts <ryan.roberts@arm.com>
Cc: Yin Fengwei <fengwei.yin@intel.com>
Signed-off-by: Andrew Morton <akpm@linux-foundation.org>
---

 mm/ksm.c |    2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/mm/ksm.c~mm-ksm-page_remove_rmap-folio_remove_rmap_pte
+++ a/mm/ksm.c
@@ -1449,7 +1449,7 @@ static int replace_page(struct vm_area_s
 	set_pte_at_notify(mm, addr, ptep, newpte);
 
 	folio = page_folio(page);
-	page_remove_rmap(page, vma, false);
+	folio_remove_rmap_pte(folio, page, vma);
 	if (!folio_mapped(folio))
 		folio_free_swap(folio);
 	folio_put(folio);
_

